                        "form": "roupies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ecb90725-4995-3c9c-b81c-7acffbe3a53f",
                        "entry_id": "b75545f4-a4ba-3428-9c15-1513bc539f0b",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Monnaie utilisée en Inde, au Pakistan, au Sri Lanka, au Népal, à l’île Maurice, aux îles Seychelles, en Indonésie et aux Maldives. Son symbole est ₨ (Unicode U+20A8)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1ed32f3d-5920-466c-a152-1a1cb1e45cb0",
                                "sense_id": "ecb90725-4995-3c9c-b81c-7acffbe3a53f",
                                "text": "Les cinq roupies qu'il avait cachées dans son dhoti et les deux roupies qu'il venait de gagner."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b644fe38-1c0e-499c-91fc-720926c12451",
                                "sense_id": "ecb90725-4995-3c9c-b81c-7acffbe3a53f",
                                "text": "Roupie indienne. Son symbole est ₹ (Unicode U+20B9)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6edf4781-625f-4132-b3c6-df4fe4778877",
                                "sense_id": "ecb90725-4995-3c9c-b81c-7acffbe3a53f",
                                "text": "Roupie seychelloise."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b2528591-8a23-4188-b8df-5e375d18a494",
                        "source_entry_id": "b75545f4-a4ba-3428-9c15-1513bc539f0b",
                        "source_sense_id": "ecb90725-4995-3c9c-b81c-7acffbe3a53f",
                        "target_lang_word": "rupee",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "rupee",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5234aea6-3ba3-37e0-8f70-6b27ddf51f0d",
                                        "entry_id": "36029e38-d754-3e97-9a04-8806036f3f70",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The common name for the monetary currencies used in modern India, Mauritius, Nepal, Pakistan, the Seychelles, or Sri Lanka."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "44518ffb-4a3d-4efe-bd22-5a6c71ac56b9",
                                                "sense_id": "5234aea6-3ba3-37e0-8f70-6b27ddf51f0d",
                                                "text": "In fact, the visible appearance of the iron is a symbol; it is not what it ultimately is. To take an analogy we are given a ten-rupee note. He knows it truly who at sight recognizes the piece of paper as a symbol of unity that represents ten separate silver coins."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c905312-4c77-456e-a97f-3c271c6e0c98",
                                                "sense_id": "5234aea6-3ba3-37e0-8f70-6b27ddf51f0d",
                                                "text": "In the fifth and sixth [standard] I obtained scholarships of rupees four and ten respectively, an achievement for which I have to thank good luck more than my merit."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "655a7048-d515-4b16-b764-5c029fc1f298",
                                                "sense_id": "5234aea6-3ba3-37e0-8f70-6b27ddf51f0d",
                                                "text": "There are no precise estimates available about the capital requirements of agricultural and rural development in India. But the amount required is in hundreds of thousands of crores of rupees."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15b6425c-a0b9-4d98-b10e-de81a5e9cc6a",
                                                "sense_id": "5234aea6-3ba3-37e0-8f70-6b27ddf51f0d",
                                                "text": "The Seychelles rupee was allowed to depreciate in 2006 after being overvalued for years and fell by 10% in the first 9 months of 2007. Despite these actions, the Seychelles economy has struggled to maintain its gains and in 2008 suffered from food and oil price shocks, a foreign exchange shortage, high inflation, large financing gaps, and the global recession."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8452e235-5d84-4d57-b41b-0c0105929d91",
                                                "sense_id": "5234aea6-3ba3-37e0-8f70-6b27ddf51f0d",
                                                "text": "Sadhana and Sanjeev Prasad, who live in Haridwar, a city in northern Uttarakhand state, filed a petition this month seeking 50 million Indian rupees (about $643,000) in damages from their son, 35, and his wife, 31."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2c5298e9-0533-3d3e-94ff-892b03937072",
                                        "entry_id": "36029e38-d754-3e97-9a04-8806036f3f70",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A silver coin circulating in India between the 16th and 20th centuries, weighing one tola (formerly 170–180 troy grains; from 1833, 180 troy grains)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "historical"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7830fbbc-ad69-4c7d-9290-19e0e95dc6b5",
                                                "sense_id": "2c5298e9-0533-3d3e-94ff-892b03937072",
                                                "text": "The only Evidence that was produced by the [East India] Company, was, a letter from Samuel Annesley, at Surrat, dated the 16th January 1694; wherein he gives this Account: Rupees. 655,000. Sent home as Cargo in the Ships Defence and Resolution."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8f116644-87a5-43a2-965a-0034b8cbffd2",
                                                "sense_id": "2c5298e9-0533-3d3e-94ff-892b03937072",
                                                "text": "The roupie, as the French write it, roupee, or rupee, as it is ſpelt in our authors, is a ſilver coin, ſomething broader than one of our ſhillings, and much thicker; in point of fineneſs, it is better than the Engliſh ſtandard; for its weight is 7 dwt. 11 gr. which, reduced to our ſtandard, would be 7 dwt. 13 mt. ²⁄₂²⁄₆¹⁄₆³⁄₄."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebd01e9c-73c9-4d20-8f46-34d6aaeae9d6",
                                                "sense_id": "2c5298e9-0533-3d3e-94ff-892b03937072",
                                                "text": "How much do you pay for a wife? Nine rupees and a half. / Why don't you give ten? It is not our custom. / Do you ever pay a smaller sum for a wife than nine rupees and a half? Sometimes, we conclude the bargain for eight rupees."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7b69e6ca-7800-3674-bf0c-8741b8418795",
                                        "entry_id": "36029e38-d754-3e97-9a04-8806036f3f70",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The primary currency of Hyrule."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
